Subject: [PATCH] jasmine-j0139: CPU idle states through PSCI CPU_SUSPEND (power plan item 3)

The cores only ever did WFI. This adds the stock sdm660 lpm-levels states through PSCI
CPU_SUSPEND (extended StateID: cpu ret 0x2, cpu pc 0x40000003, cpu + L2 pc 0x41000043),
default off. A power-collapsed core resumes through sweet_secondary_entry -> reset_vector ->
resume_idle_cpu -> arm_init_idle_cpu -> cpu_idle_exit(TRUE) (XNU's non-retention idle path);
sweet_cpu_idle_resumed restores the GIC CPU interface and the timer compare. The core's timer
is lost in pc, so the QTimer frame 0 physical timer (SPI 8 = INTID 40, routed to the first
Silver core) is a broadcast timer: a core going down publishes its deadline, the handler
IPIs it when due. pc only when the next timer is >= PC_US away (default 2000) and the CPU is
in the pc mask (default 0xFE: not the boot CPU).

Also: mode 0 can skip XNU's L1 flush before every WFI (platform_cache_idle_enter, meant for
non-coherent ARMv7), `cpuidle flush 0|1`, default 1 = old behaviour.

Command port: `cpuidle` shows mode, per-CPU entries/time per state, PSCI results and
broadcast counters; `cpuidle MODE [PC_US [MASK]] [force]` (0 wfi, 1 ret, 2 + core pc,
3 + core and L2 pc), `cpuidle flush 0|1`, `cpuidle reset`.
---
